($t$Swietenia mahagoni$t$, $t$Swietenia mahagoni$t$, $t$Meliaceae$t$, $t$Famiglia botanica: Meliaceae. Portamento: Tree. Altezza massima indicativa: 25 m. Swietenia mahagoni or Mahogany is an evergreen or briefly deciduous tree commonly found in Southeastern part of North America. It grows up to 30-35 m tall with a large, round crown and short bole that can be up to 100 cm in diameter. The leaves are pinnate with four to eight leaflets each. The flowers are small and produced in panicles. The fruits are woody capsule containing plenty of winged seeds. No plant part is edible. Decoction of the stem bark is taken orally against diarrhea and dysentery, and used to induce hemorrhage. Bark decoction is used externally to dress wounds caused by firearms. Though often used as a shade tree, Mahogany is also used primarily for its high-quality wood. It is medium-weight, highly durable, resistant to most wood-rotting fungi, and easy to work. It is used commonly for high-quality furniture, joinery, boars, carvings, musical instruments, etc. Seeds yield oil which has commercial uses.$t$, $j${"luce": "Pieno sole", "acqua": "Moderata", "terreno": "Tollera terreno: medio, argilloso/pesante"}$j$::jsonb, ARRAY[$t$Scheda in bozza, importata automaticamente da Plants For A Future (pfaf.org): dati non verificati manualmente, da controllare prima di considerarli affidabili$t$, $t$Nome comune (inglese, fonte PFAF): Mahogany, West Indies Mahogany$t$, $t$Rischi segnalati dalla fonte (testo originale in inglese, non tradotto per non alterarne il significato): None known$t$], $j${"irrigazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "concimazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "potatura": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "npk": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}}$j$::jsonb, $j${"famiglia_botanica": "Meliaceae", "giorni_germinazione": null, "giorni