($t$Tectona grandis$t$, $t$Tectona grandis$t$, $t$Lamiaceae$t$, $t$Famiglia botanica: Lamiaceae. Portamento: Tree. Altezza massima indicativa: 30 m. Found in East Asia, Tectona grandis or commonly known as Teak is a tropical, flowering, deciduous tree up to 40 m tall and 1 m in bole diameter. It has an open crown and its bole is often buttressed. The flowers are fragrant, white, and small. Same as the large, ovate-elliptic, papery leaves, it is often hairy on the lower surface. Fruits are globose. Teak is highly valued for its wood which is of superior quality. Highly durable and water resistant, it is used for boat building, exterior construction, veneer, furniture ,carving, etc. The leaves are used for fermenting soybeans. Teak is mainly propagated by seeds.$t$, $j${"luce": "Pieno sole", "acqua": "Moderata", "terreno": "Tollera terreno: sabbioso/leggero, medio, argilloso/pesante"}$j$::jsonb, ARRAY[$t$Scheda in bozza, importata automaticamente da Plants For A Future (pfaf.org): dati non verificati manualmente, da controllare prima di considerarli affidabili$t$, $t$Nome comune (inglese, fonte PFAF): Teak$t$, $t$Rischi segnalati dalla fonte (testo originale in inglese, non tradotto per non alterarne il significato): The fine dust produced in machining operations may cause irritation of the skin or bronchial asthma and rhinitis after inhalation; a well-functioning dust extractor fan is recommended. The substance responsible for the allergic reaction is probably the naphthoquinone desoxylapachol[299 ].$t$], $j${"irrigazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "concimazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "potatura": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "npk": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}}$j$::jsonb, $j${"famiglia_botanica": "Lamiaceae", "giorni_germinazione": null, "giorni_trapianto": null, "giorni_raccolta": null, "fi